      "title": "Whom does Theo represent?",
      "narration": "Theo has just joined AMG and holds a Maryland producer license. Under agency law, the insurer is the principal and the producer is its agent. The producer acts on the insurer’s behalf, and the insurer is responsible for acts within the producer’s authority. A captive producer represents a single insurer. An independent producer represents several. Maryland uses one license, insurance producer, for people who historically were called agents or brokers. Whatever the label, when a producer sells an insurer’s policy, the insurer is the party whose authority is being exercised.",
